{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 32, :comments ["<b>Under the staff.</b> When one comes to tithe them, he brings them out through the opening one after another, and the tither strikes them with a staff painted with סִקְרָא, so that it be recognizable that it is tithe — thus he does for lambs and calves of every single year (cf. N.H.)." "<b>It shall be holy.</b> To offer its blood and its emurim on the altar, and the flesh is eaten by the owners — for it is not counted among the rest of the priestly gifts, nor do we find that its flesh is given to the priests."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {0 "סִקְרָא is Aramaic for a red/dyed color; the parenthetical (בכו' נ\"ח) abbreviates a cross-reference, here rendered '(cf. N.H.)'."}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:09:02.842987862Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}